erprise for small  business people and working people David  is joining us from Baltimore good  morning welcome to the conversation  David good morning senator Sam  I remember watching a video of you on  YouTube where you were questioning Ben  Bernanke of the Federal Reserve and  being completely astounded when you  asked him where the people's money went  if he could tell you exactly where it  went him and he straight up said no to  you I just that really struck true to me  about how secretive and how powerful the  Federal Reserve is but getting to some  of your comments earlier you have  continued to speak about the greed of  Wall Street and the big business and big  corporations however the greed that I  see that is actually destroying the  country right now is the greed in  Washington of you perhaps yourself but  maybe not yourself but certainly your  colleagues there in the Senate and in  the house you guys continue to spend a  lot more money way too much money more  than what the federal government  legitimately brings in every single  month and you guys want to always raise  taxes on the whip on the wealthy or  whoever to cover the expenses of your  increased spending in Washington why  can't the federal government simply live  within its means why can't you guys  simply spend what you take in every  single month which I've heard is around  two hundred billion dollars a month  thank you David okay David let me answer  you you talked about the Fed yes I did  ask Bernanke where the trillions of  dollars went he said he refused he  refused to tell me we introduced  legislation to make him tell me that  legislation was included in the  financial reform bill and eventually  that came out and that was less just  what I was talking about a month ago  three trillion dollars going to every  financial institution logic in this  country many large corporations many  individuals as well in terms of spending  within our means yes i agree i ran a  city for eight years we took in money we  spent the same amount as we took in we  had a balanced budget should we be doing  that yeah but when you're in the midst  of a recession and you have a whole lot  of people who are hurting there are  investments that you have to make it is  wrong  my view to say that we should be  throwing hundreds of thousands of kids  off of heads thought for one example of  many so to answer your question is that  a budget is two things it is spending it  is bringing in review I do believe as I  said a number of times this morning it  is absurd to give tax breaks to people  who don't need it and then cut back on  programs for people who are desperately  dependent upon those programs senator  Bernie Sanders independent from Vermont  and out with a new book from his speech  on December the 10th that we covered on  c-span to the speech a historic  filibuster on corporate greed and the  decline of our middle class thanks as  always for being with us good to be with  you appreciate your time coming up in  just a couple minutes we're going to  introduce you to our grand prize winner  and c-span's student cam contest and  also more information on many of the  entries but first to look at the latest  news from c-span radio it's 28 past the  hour this just in the Board of NPR news  has fired CEO Vivian Schiller in the  wake of a video sting by a conservative  activist and US Vice President Joe Biden  speaking to business leaders in Russia  to a management school calling on Russia  to attack corruption and improve its  legal system the vice president also  supporting Russia's attempts to join the  World Trade Organization and while the  vice president travels in Russia  President Obama and first lady Michelle  here in Washington and today they've  posted a video on facebook to promote a  bullying prevention conference that  they'll host at the White House tomorrow  in a taped video message the president  says that bullying should no longer be  treated as an unavoidable par